RaceDay Data Dictionary

1. Introduction

This data dictionary provides an overview of the main entities planned for the RaceDay database.

The database design currently contains six main entities:

Users
Events
Categories
Enrolments
Results
Routes

The data dictionary supports the Entity Relationship Diagram and SQL database design created for Part 1.



2. Users

Stores information about people using the RaceDay system.

Field	Description
UserID	Unique identifier for a user
Name	User’s name
Email	User’s email address
Password	User authentication information
Role	Identifies whether the user is an Organiser or Participant



3. Events

Stores information about sporting events.

Field	Description
EventID	Unique identifier for an event
EventName	Name of the event
EventDate	Date of the event
Location	Location where the event takes place
OrganiserID	Identifies the Organiser responsible for the event



4. Categories

Stores categories available for an event.

Field	Description
CategoryID	Unique identifier for a category
CategoryName	Name of the category
EventID	Identifies the event associated with the category



5. Enrolments

Stores participant enrolments in events.

Field	Description
EnrolmentID	Unique identifier for an enrolment
UserID	Identifies the Participant
EventID	Identifies the selected event
CategoryID	Identifies the selected category
EnrolmentDate	Date the participant enrolled



6. Results

Stores participant performance results.

Field	Description
ResultID	Unique identifier for a result
EnrolmentID	Identifies the enrolment associated with the result
FinishTime	Participant’s recorded finishing time
Position	Participant’s finishing position



7. Routes

Stores information about event routes.

Field	Description
RouteID	Unique identifier for a route
EventID	Identifies the event associated with the route
RouteName	Name or description of the route
Distance	Distance of the route



8. Relationships

The main database relationships are:

One Organiser can manage many Events.
One Event can contain many Categories.
One Event can have many Enrolments.
One Participant can have many Enrolments.
One Category can have many Enrolments.
One Enrolment can have zero or one Result.
One Event can have zero or one Route.



9. Part 2

The data dictionary represents the planned database structure for Part 1.

Fields and database structures may be expanded or refined during Part 2 as the RaceDay application is developed.
